Subject: [flexcounter] hand the poll cycle start and collection time to plugins

Backport of nexthop-ai/private-sonic-sairedis#340 (NOS-15253), ported to this
tree: the upstream 202511 FlexCounter.cpp has diverged from the fork the PR was
authored against, so the hunks were re-derived against the pinned source. The
code change is identical.

A plugin that wants the real poll cadence can only stamp its own clock, and it
runs inside runPlugins() -- after collectCounters(). Consecutive stamps therefore
differ by the cycle period plus the change in collection time, so stat-collection
jitter is indistinguishable from poll jitter.

Adds two optional, positional plugin arguments:
  ARGV[4] - monotonic cycle start, captured before collectCounters()
  ARGV[5] - stat collection time for this cycle

Both are additive; existing plugins read no further than ARGV[3] and are
unaffected. Poll scheduling behaviour is unchanged -- the sleep correction is
still computed from start to finish exactly as before.

Upstream: https://github.com/nexthop-ai/private-sonic-sairedis/pull/340

